{
	"doc": "Hunters drawn on Meshy's own skeleton and clips (scripts/heroes/warden_native.gd, docs/art/wardens/MESHY_NATIVE.md), keyed by art name. meshy_native: the switch (off = the contract model as before; Albert and Vex are listed off until their <art>_meshy.glb is packed and picked). Size: Meshy's head bone onto the rig's head pivot (WardenNative._fit). file: art/wardens/<art>/<art>_meshy.glb. clips: game state -> Meshy clip, plus optional slots (lmb, lmb_hold, rmb, e, r, dash, glide, land, hit, downed, stomp; MESHY_NATIVE.md, Clip slots): a missing one plays today's clip. walk_mps/run_mps/crouch_mps: m/s ground speed each loop plays at rate 1; run_from: m/s where the walk hands to the run; attack_rate, jump_rate: play rate of those one-shots. hand: Meshy's bone the weapon's aim node rides. anchors: anchor empty -> the Meshy bone it rides. crouch_arms_from: the crouch plays that state's clip on the arms (the bones below arm_roots, default LeftShoulder and RightShoulder): Meshy's crouch holds a torch out. toon (default true): the game's hero-toon pass on the surfaces. bones: contract bone -> this Hunter's Meshy bone, for WardenSkeleton.find (Cinder's heel jets on her feet; the 14 contract bones need none: WardenSkeleton.NATIVE). orbits: orbit node of the contract .glb -> the Meshy bone it rides (the props are copied from <art>.glb and turn as on the contract path: Tenzo's seeing-stones). props: contract bone -> material names of the contract model's parts Meshy's mesh lacks, hung on Meshy's bones (WardenProps: Kael's sword, Cinder's heel jets); tilt: contract bone -> degrees its part bends back toward the limb (Kael's blade: his contract rest holds it 47 deg ahead of the arm, his own idle clip bends the wrist; Meshy's clips do not). own_casts: her casts and recoils play no Meshy swing (her hands cast: kmoves rows). clip_files, kmoves: the Hunter's own clips for kit moves (WardenNativeMoves; Cinder's art/wardens/cinder/cinder_clips.glb from tools/meshy/cinder_native_clips.py): kit move id -> {clip, then (loops after clip), hold (last pose stays), upper (a layer over the legs' clip: torso, head and arms only)}. stretch {kmove, y, rest}: those parts' length along their bone while that kit move plays and otherwise (as the contract clips key Cinder's jet bones: x3 in Flue Flight, x0.06 at rest).",
